
  <sn><md>### `#define` in C

`#define` is a **preprocessor directive** in C used to define a **macro**.

**Definition:** `#define` tells the C preprocessor to replace a specified identifier with a particular sequence of tokens before the actual compilation begins.

</md></sn>
